{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR in the 10-20 day horizon during the observed downtrend, failing to capture the magnitude of the collapse from ~85 to ~67.",
    "Eliminate artificial mean reversion: The model forecasts a flat or slightly rising trajectory (mean reversion) regardless of the sharp downward momentum in history; adjust forecasts to follow the prevailing trend rather than reverting to a static mean.",
    "Reduce lag in trend identification: The model reacts too slowly to the initial price drop (starting around day 3-4 of the forecast), resulting in significant overestimation in the first week; incorporate a faster decay factor for recent negative price changes.",
    "Ignore neutral sentiment signals: Sentiment scores of 0.00 or low values (0.33) during a downtrend do not trigger the necessary bearish adjustment in the model; treat low sentiment as a confirmation of downward pressure rather than a neutral baseline.",
    "Adjust for volatility clustering: The model fails to anticipate the secondary dip and subsequent volatility (e.g., the drop to 66.73); forecasts should be more responsive to the increasing variance in the tail of the distribution."
  ]
}
